{
  "case_id": "2020-20-512",
  "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have two questions. The first one is, what is it precisely that you are complaining about in this Court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Waxman, let me put on the table some of what is said by those who challenge your idea of amateurism. The briefs that are supported -- that are submitted in support of the Respondents paint a pretty stark picture, and they argue that colleges with powerhouse football and basketball programs are really exploiting the students that they recruit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought, Mr. Waxman, that the district court's injunction only prohibits the NCAA from limiting education-related expenses. It does not prohibit the conference from doing so. So, if your priority is maintaining amateurism in college athletics and you and your members think that increasing education-related benefits will undermine the spirit of amateurism, why don't the conferences impose those limits?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. WAXMAN",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the fact that we may -- that school -- under her decree, schools may provide $5,980 per year to every Division I athlete just for being on a team."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I get your point MR. WAXMAN: -- internships?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: -- when you answered and you said it's not pay because the NCAA has defined \"pay\" as the reasonable and necessary expenses to obtain education. But I'm wondering, why does the NCAA get to define what pay is?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. WAXMAN",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our definition, which has been stable over decades, long predating Board of Regents, is that it is -- you're not being paid to play if you receive an allowance for the actual and necessary expenses of your education, whether those expenses be --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. WAXMAN",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "if schools were, in fact, required to make the kind of payments that the district judge imposed in her final decree, schools would -- I mean, they have to come up with the money somewhere, the -- you know, the -- the $6,000 a year amounts to seven -- $735 million per year that schools have to come up with in addition to the -- the retrospective treble damages awards. And the -- the evidence was that schools would, per force, reduce the number of \"non-revenue sports,\" men's and women's sports, thus reducing the advantages and offerings available to student-athletes in those other sports."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. KESSLER",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The naked horizontal monopsony restraints that the competing NCAA schools have adopted in these labor markets would be per se unlawful in any other context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice THOMAS",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Briefly, Mr. Kessler, the -- just following up on what you just said, what if you have a consumer survey that suggests tomorrow that the consumers think it's fine for amateur athletes to make $20,000 a year? Would we be back in court with litigation suggest -- about"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think, if we really have a case here, it's a tough case for me, and the reason it's so tough is -- for me is because this is not an ordinary product. This is an effort to bring into the world something that's brought joy and all kinds of things to --to millions and millions of people, and it's only partly economic. Okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kessler",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I believe it was substantially less restrictive, Your Honor, because it allowed the NCAA to continue to impose all of its restraints on compensation not related to education, and it said that what it can't justify, what it can't do, is just education-related restraint, but the reason we know it's substantially less restrictive is because there are life-changing benefits for these athletes that will be provided."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court here found as a matter of fact that the NCAA's restraints on education-related benefits cannot be justified as reasonable, necessary -- reasonably necessary to maintain demand for college sports or define the NCAA's product."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kessler",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress, not the courts. The rule of reason already provides ample latitude to joint ventures, to organizations like this, to sports leagues, to assert what you need to assert to justify the restraints you need."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you have any thoughts about that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What's your response to that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Prelogar",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0004-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the Ninth Circuit considered this argument expressly and said that interpreting the injunction to authorize sham payments or illegitimate benefits is -- is -- is not an accurate representation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On this record, do you think a district court could have set limits that were significantly higher than the limits that were set by the district court here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Petitioners are wrong to argue that any restrictions related to their conception of amateurism, including their horizontal price-fixing agreements, must be upheld without analysis rather than applying the rule of reason. That would be an extraordinary departure from traditional antitrust principles."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0004-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 89,
        "start": 89
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Gorsuch, monopsony power does not take away the producer's right to define the product any more for the NCAA than, for example, for the Little League, which eight years ago got $80 million for its television contract."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-20-512",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a88c5515ceb56a0f0aeac0d23e37cd8c54df9e352fa5f8d0f15e05b508711960",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a88c5515ceb5-0004-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
